a0327535c7c\n    03_Matters/beacon-instant-onboarding/documents/batch-valid.txt: 608f10911744be873ac5a3b66e7eea9fb0519f54a5f3fd0e238d80975586add7\n    03_Matters/beacon-instant-onboarding/documents/partial-settlement-notes.pdf.extracted.md: 155f16d6436361040fac12b98ffcb5daa85c2f1b46302c261e3941c4d1c37ca3\n    03_Matters/beacon-instant-onboarding/documents/partial-settlement-notes.pdf: 82566301606e15b7675e9287a9743cddf3c33a7c8c140e39ac679c3bf2f3181f\n    business_question: 2a600fd29efcc847f78b2b7e:4ea9fcd39b7b54f5a129d35cebd0a0b7d1897b4db9ef7ee57518f6ea012c1bcc\nrecommendation_version_id: null\nrecommendation_snapshot: '# Recommendations\n\n\n  No recommendation yet. Intake must distinguish deposit onboarding, credit decisioning,\n  fraud review, and partner-required manual review.'\nreview:\n  segments:\n  - kind: equal\n    text: '## Recommendation\n\n\n      Beacon can proceed toward launching the revised onboarding flow for the low-risk\n      segment, **conditional on confirming partner approval before go-live**. The\n      change applies only to the low-risk segment and uses identity and fraud signals,\n      so the scope is narrow. Do not launch until the partner approval requirement\n      is confirmed and the non-approval path is settled.\n\n\n      ## Next product steps\n\n\n      - Confirm with the partner whether approval is required before the revised flow\n      launches.\n\n      - Decide the notice/explanation path for applicants the automation cannot approve\n      (e.g., direct them to contact support).\n\n      - Confirm the legal characterization of the automated decision and the notice\n      that follows a non-approval.\n\n\n      ## Evidence and open facts\n\n\n      - Reported facts: the change applies only to the low-risk segment; the flow\n      uses identity and fraud signals.\n\n      - Open: whether partner approval constrains the rollout; what notice or explanation\n      follows a non-approval; the legal characterization of the automated decision.\n\n      - No external authority was retrieved for this preview; the memo reflects the\n      current business question and reported facts only.\n\n      '\n    change_id: ''\n    author_id: ''\n    author_name: ''\n    author_color: ''\n    created_at: ''\n  comments: []\n  version: 2\n  tracking: false\n  authors: []\n  comment_events: []\n---\n## Recommendation\n\nBeacon can proceed toward launching the revised onboarding flow for the low-risk segment, **conditional on confirming partner approval before go-live**. The change applies only to the low-risk segment and uses identity and fraud signals, so the scope is narrow. Do not launch until the partner approval requirement is confirmed and the non-approval path is settled.\n\n## Next product steps\n\n- Confirm with the partner whether approval is required before the revised flow launches.\n- Decide the notice/explanation path for applicants the automation cannot approve (e.g., direct them to contact support).\n- Confirm the legal characterization of the automated decision and the notice that follows a non-approval.\n\n## Evidence and open facts\n\n- Reported facts: the change applies only to the low-risk segment; the flow uses identity and fraud signals.\n- Open: whether partner approval constrains the rollout; what notice or explanation follows a non-approval; the legal characterization of the automated decision.\n- No external authority was retrieved for this preview; the memo reflects the current business question and reported facts only.\n",
